BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sabbath Lives Halloween Party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T223000
UID:6ac4721aead9596b9f605cde@squarespace.com
DESCRIPTION:It’s a Halloween Party celebrating the Prince of Darkness!\n
 Don't miss this special Halloween performance of Sabbath Lives in Occident
 al.\nWell known throughout the Bay Area\, Sabbath Lives recreates the clas
 sic\, heavy\, and blues-infused sound of the godfathers of heavy metal\, f
 ocusing on accurate guitar tones\, raw power\, and iconic Ozzy-era anthems
 . With Tom Finch\, Kalyan Godden\, Dana Miller and Troy Bradley.\nIt's Hal
 loween so dress up! Cash prize for best costume.\nDoors at 7:30\, Show at 
 8:00 PM. Refreshments/beer/wine for sale\, free parking. Limited seating\,
  first come.\n$25 GA\, discount for members.\nGet Tickets\nTroy Bradley\n-
  has been singing in the Bay Area for over 30 years with bands like dysfun
 ctional family and Sabbath lives. He has sung with many local guitar heroe
 s such as Josh Zee\, Eric McFadden and Tom Finch\, to name a few. Troy is 
 originally from Huntington Beach where he formed his first punk/metal band
  called funeral of dreams before moving to the Bay Area in the early 90s w
 here he has been singing ever since.\nDana Miller\n- Drummer\, has played 
 with multiple local rock bands\, including local legends liquid sky and 2 
 Lane blacktop. Dana recorded an album with producer Bill Bottrell in the 9
 0s and has played on multiple sessions and records\, including English pop
  duo Alisha’s Attic for Mercury records which placed a song on the sound
 track of the hit\, Bridget Jones‘s diary.\nTom Finch\n- a California nat
 ive and Guitarist for over 45 years is Influenced by rock\, blues\, and ja
 zz styles. A Gulf Coast Music Hall of Fame inductee\, Tom has toured throu
 ghout the U.S.\, Europe\, Japan and Canada\, and is featured on many album
 s with groups such a Big Brother & the Holding Co\, Jazz Iguanas & Pamela 
 Parker as well as leading his own groups. Tom has played with a variety of
  artists some of which include: Jefferson Starship\, Joan Baez\, Norton Bu
 ffalo\, Steve Smith and many more!\nKalyan Godden\n- a California native a
 nd multi-instrumentalist for more than 30 years\, he plays bass\, guitar\,
  and sarode. Primarily a bass player he has played with many bay area grou
 ps such as\, Bent Again\, The Holdouts\, Burl\, 5MO\, Roots Foundation\, R
 ed-I\, The Beautiful Losers\, Prozak and Sabbath Lives\, in genres spannin
 g grunge\, rock\, reggae \,and metal. When he is not playing music he can 
 be found repairing or building a wide range of instruments\, from guitars 
 to sitars and everything in between.
LOCATION:Occidental Center for the Arts\, 3850 Doris Murphy Court\, Occide
 ntal
URL:https://www.occidentalcenterforthearts.org/upcoming-events/sabbath-liv
 es-halloween-party
X-SOURCE:Occidental Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
